      "description": "The Entrance Hall. In 1872, The 7th Duke commissioned the Scottish architect, David Bryce, to design a Baronial entrance hall. This was part of the Duke’s scheme to convert the Georgian mansion back to a castle. The weapon display includes targes (shields) and muskets which were used at the Battle of Culloden.",
