      "credit": "Own work",
      "source": "Blair interior sca11",
      "description": "The Ballroom at Blair Castle. Commissioned by the 7th Duke, the Ballroom was designed by David Bryce for the Atholl Highlanders. The celebrated fiddler, Niel Gow was closely associated with the 2nd, 3rd and 4th Dukes and his portrait by Sir Henry Raeburn, his chair and fiddle are displayed on the stage. The Ballroom hosts many Highland balls, wedding receptions, corporate hospitality and private dinners, as well as the Atholl Highlanders’ annual ball.",
